{
  "_doc": [
    "The map's outline sources. The app reads each source's link rules (and name, kind) to link its appellations and",
    "vineyards to their outlines (Settings › Maintenance › Shape links, run after the map pack is installed); the rest",
    "(files, id, name, level, id_prefix, display_merge_m, assume_crs...) is how the published outlines were built.",
    "A shape's link is '<name>:<id>'.",
    "link: table (appellations or vineyards) and by: an id column of it (strip_prefix: only values starting with it, prefix",
    "removed; region: the row's region before the id, region_aliases renaming some or naming several files' keys: an id",
    "in more than one takes the shape with the row's name, else isn't linked), or 'name' with country (the appellation's",
    "name as a slug, Australia's aliases applied), or 'store_name': the shape's own name in the store within the row's",
    "country (country_codes; for ids like PDO-IT-A1234), only when the when_empty column is empty, aliases ('Country /",
    "our name': source_id) first: same denomination, other spelling or renamed / merged (checked by hand).",
    "'country_name': the shape's id is '<country>:<appellation name>' (the admin areas). store_name with 'country': a",
    "one-country source whose ids don't carry it (INAO, France); inao_denom comes first: a French name with its own INAO",
    "outline (Gevrey-Chambertin premier cru) takes it before the INAO id, which the village and its premier crus share.",
    "link can be a list of rules. A row is linked to the first rule, in this order, that finds its shape.",
    "vineyard: INAO's premiers crus. An installation's own sources go in data/geo/sources.local.json (same format): one",
    "named like a source here replaces it, others are added.",
    "lieu_dit: the cadastre's lieux-dits touching AOC vines (geo_scripts/etl_lieux_dits.py, a file per departement), ids",
    "'<commune>:<slug>'; detail_columns: kept as JSON in the store's details column (the village, the appellations its",
    "land is eligible for, most specific first, its share of vines). No link rule: a vineyard is linked to one when",
    "a wine is (Settings › Maintenance › Lieux-dits for your wines)."
  ],
